they are NOT false positives from this cause. They carry the `[health]` prefix, i.e. the launchd `watch` path, for which a fire is not an ancestor and which never calls `dashboard()`; and the 900 KB control above shows that observer can match a fire’s argv. **Check 3 is SOUND.**** 🎯 **What earns it a cure is the DIRECTION at the one moment it fires: §2.0c cost 37h50m across 35 fires to establish that a fire MUST read this panel, and the panel’s `fire :` row was the one line guaranteed wrong for its prescribed reader — stating, affirmatively, that no fire is running at the exact moment one is. That fails toward “the lock is unowned”, the lock-stealing direction §1.1 exists to prevent. The cost is zero only because §1.1 binds on the `FIRE END` log signal rather than on this row.** 🛠️ **CURED AT THE SITE so it cannot rot out of sync with prose: the row now DECLARES and does NOT refuse (F-2366-1’s choice for BUSY) — exit codes untouched — keying on `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, the house fire-shell discriminator `playwright.config.ts`’s `isFireShell` already uses (§3.1, guarded by `fire-shell-serialisation.test.mjs`): `fire   : RUNNING (you, the caller) — pgrep cannot see its own ancestors…`. **GATED, never always-on**: an unconditional line names a blind spot an idle board does not have, which is how a declaration decays into a formality.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/health-watch-fire-line-guard.test.mjs` — 7 arms, 47 ms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; `gate-caller-audit` PASS. EXTRACTION-based (the `main-lock-gate-guard` house pattern) because running the real `dashboard()` fires three `curl` edge probes at up to 10 s each, and it REFUSES rather than passing vacuously if its subject block is gone (F-2217-1).** 🔬 **TEETH, 9 variants manufactured IN PLACE with the subject restored BYTE-IDENTICALLY (sha256-asserted) after every one: ALL 7 ARMS red under at least one SUBSTANTIVE variant, so none is decoration — over-general always-on reds **3 and 5** (exactly the two reverse control