📈 **F-2620-2 — `test:ledger-guards` RE-MEASURED AT `210.5 s` ON A QUIET BOARD, `25%` ABOVE THE BAND THE LAW BANKS, AND THE ASSERTION GROWTH DOES NOT EXPLAIN IT (measured s2620; restated at the site in `scripts/fire.md`, which is what that clause asks for).** F-2414-1 ends *"Derive the counts when you need them … and re-state them here when you do"*, so this is the prescribed act rather than a drive-by. 📊 **MEASURED: `1170` node assertions (`0` crosses) plus `83` bash legs, THREE runs, all `rc=0`, wall **`210.5 s`**, **`214.3 s`** and **`254.1 s`** — a `21%` spread — routed through `node` per §2.0d. The board was as quiet as this factory gets — DRY both ways for the 88th consecutive fire, runner ALIVE but idle, no drain, no lane work, no arena, and nothing else of mine running (the `347.2 s` gazette sweep had finished six minutes earlier).** **The sequence is now assertions `97 → 180 → 948 → 1064 → 1140 → 1170` and quiet wall `15.3 → 49.9 → 77–99 → 114–155 → 123–168 → 210.5 s`.** ⚠️ **THE HONEST READING, AND I WILL NOT DRESS IT UP: assertions grew `+2.6%` since s2590 while quiet wall grew `+25%` against the top of its band, so "it got BIGGER, not slower" — TRUE at every previous step of this sequence — does NOT account for this one.** I took THREE runs — each extra one was OWED rather than chosen, because restating this figure MUTATES A LAW SURFACE late in my own run and F-1300-4 makes the battery the last act of any fire that does so — and **the third refuted the band I had already banked from the first two.** After runs 1 and 2 (`1.8%` apart) I published `210–215 s` and called it the tightest pair this chain had recorded; run 3 landed `21%` above run 1. **I am recording that reversal rather than quietly widening the number, because the reversal is the finding.** The observed quiet range is `210–254 s`, every reading is a FLOOR and not a bound, and the CAUSE remains **UNMEASURED and deliberately not guessed** (F-2182-1). ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATEL