📐 **F-2618-1 — A SURVIVAL BOUND IS A *STATISTIC* BEFORE IT IS A NUMBER, AND TWO CONSECUTIVE FIRES PUBLISHED THE WRONG EXTREMUM: THE `/private/tmp` REAPER HAS NO AGE THRESHOLD AT ALL, AND THE BOUND THE LAW CARRIES IS 2.1× TOO SMALL *AND* MEASURES NOTHING.** F-2616-1 bounds survival from below at `2.82 d` and calls a ~3-day threshold CONSISTENT; F-2617-1 "moves the bound `2.82 → 3.87 d`" from the **NEWEST** surviving file in its subject set. 📊 **MEASURED s2618, control asserted FIRST (F-2215-1 — my walk of the 5 HOLDING trees returned **`1,874`** evidence-prefixed files, reproducing s2617's own subject count TO THE DIGIT, so any divergence is about the STATISTIC and not the population): the OLDEST survivor in that very population is `wt-boss-control/artifacts/drain-replay-control/county/reels-raw.json` at **`5.86 d` AND STILL PRESENT**. Over ALL files in the scratchpad (`64` trees, `52` holding, `12` fileless) the oldest survivor is `wt-maps/assets/pilots/map-rebuild-spike/__pycache__/*.pyc`, also `5.86 d`.** 🔑 **A NEWEST-SURVIVOR FIGURE BOUNDS NOTHING — every file in a tree is newer than its oldest, so a maximum over the surviving set is satisfied by ANY threshold. Only the MINIMUM constrains a threshold from below. Both fires computed a maximum and called it a bound.** ⛔ **AND THE THRESHOLD CANNOT SURVIVE THE DATA, PER-TREE OR PER-FILE: `wt-sprites` was reaped to FILELESS at the `2026-09-17T17:00:19Z` boundary while its OWN control `wt-sprites-control` — same boundary (`17:00:15Z`), same `2026-09-12` vintage, files spanning 19 minutes — retains all `23` at `5.84 d`. Same pass, opposite outcomes. ⓘ **THAT PAIRING IS SUPPORTING AND THE REFUTATION DOES NOT REST ON IT: `wt-sprites`’ own files are GONE, so their vintage is an INFERENCE from its control tree, labelled one (F-2182-1). The MEASURED argument is `wt-maps` ALONE — no threshold at or below `5.86 d` can be the rule when one tree carries `5.86 d` files ACROSS a pass, whatever the emptied tree held.** Six trees retain files at `5.79`–`5.86 d` (`wt-maps` 4,432 · `wt-boss-control` 36 · `wt-sprites-control` 23 · `wt-maps-control` 15 · `wt-boss` 3 · `wt-maps-evidence-aside` 1), and `wt-maps`'s NEWEST file is `2026-09-14T03:34Z`, three days BEFORE that boundary — so those 4,432 files demonstrably SURVIVED a pass. **AGE DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE WHO IS EMPTIED.**** ⓘ **MECHANISM STILL UNMEASURED AND DELIBERATELY NOT GUESSED (F-2182-1): `/etc/periodic/daily` is ABSENT exactly as F-2607-1 and F-2616-1 recorded; what is measured is the EFFECT, the `17:00 UTC` daily clustering, and now that age is not its key.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY HONEST AND NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing lost, NOT a false green, and **F-2607-1's CONCLUSION IS UNTOUCHED AND STRENGTHENED** — the fuse is real (a tree in this very scratchpad went fileless yesterday) and the arena sweep is still not deferrable. Every prior reading was TRUE about the file it named.** 🎯 **What earns it a correction is that both clauses converted a WARNING into a NUMBER A FIRE CAN BUDGET AGAINST, and it is unsupported in BOTH directions: `wt-sprites` lost everything younger than `5.86 d`, `wt-maps` still holds files older than it.** ➡️ **BINDING: there is NO age from which a fire may compute how long a `/tmp` tree has. Treat every such tree as reapable at the next `17:00 UTC` boundary whatever its file ages. If you re-measure the bound, take the MINIMUM over survivors and SAY SO.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, restraint INHERITED: the reaper is a LAWFUL external condition on a machine this factory does not control, so a red fires during ordinary correct operation and is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1) — exactly what F-2607-1 and F-2616-1 both concluded; and "did a fire take a min or a max?" is unobservable to every battery (the F-2567-1 reason). CURED AT THE SITE in `scripts/fire.md` §2E.** 💡 **REUSABLE — a NEW AXIS after *how WIDE* (F-2358-1), *which AXIS* (F-2389-1), *which TREE* (F-2484-1), *registry vs census* (F-2485-1), *entries v