ge day **`2026-09-16` holds `70` first-parent commits and has no digest**; so the first fire after 06:00 on 09-17 owes EXACTLY ONE day with no backlog behind it.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: a lag above 1 is LAWFUL and routine — an outage, a quiet night, a machine asleep — and at `4 of 63` (6.3%) a red would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate). Same restraint F-2391-1 and F-2562-2 each took for this very duty, and the reason F-2351-1 shipped LB-01's freshness probe ADVISORY at exit 0.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS: every prior finding in this chain asks whether an artifact or a subject set is THERE — empty, narrowed, stale, unreadable, wrong-tree, wrong-window. THIS ONE ASKS WHETHER IT WAS ON TIME. Presence and punctuality are different properties, and an artifact that records only WHAT it covers erases WHEN it arrived the moment it lands. When a duty's value is time-sensitive, ask what in the artifact witnesses its own filing date — and if the answer is "nothing", the lateness is unobservable by construction.**

