sured rather than lazy: the subject is a PROSE STEP, and "does this instruction name a real artifact?" is a judgement over free text — a red would fire on every honest forward-looking sentence and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate), the same restraint F-2450-1 took for a live instruction and F-2594-1 for this very duty one fire earlier.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the RUNG UNDER F-2594-1 rather than a repeat of it: that finding showed a COMPOUND resolution can be half-carried so the carried half vouches for the wrong half. THIS step's referent was never measured BY ANYONE — the duty's FACTS had been pre-flighted twice (s2594 checked the mint command's argv shape; I checked its `opensAt`) and its INSTRUCTIONS never had been. **A dated duty accumulates verified facts and unverified verbs, and the verbs are what a fire executes on the day. When a trigger approaches, do not re-check the facts — TYPE THE STEPS.**

