* · declare-only-on-failure reds **9 ALONE** · refusal-off-stdout reds **7 ALONE** · floor-count-on-a-refusal reds **8 ALONE** · dropping the CLI arg-count check reds **11 ALONE**. 🚨 **The one that matters is the OVER-GENERAL cure — "stop counting floor movements" — which silences a real determinism regression and reds arms 3/4/5 ALONE; those three reverse controls exist so that cure cannot pass.** ⚠️ **ONE METHOD NOTE PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE: my first teeth pass reddened arm 11 with NOTHING, i.e. scored it candidate decoration — because every variant mutated the compare MODULE while arm 11's subject is the CLI's argument parsing in the OTHER file. A reachability audit is scoped to the files you actually mutate, and an arm its variants cannot reach is indistinguishable from an arm with no teeth.** 💡 **REUSABLE: a drift counter that sums PROVENANCE and CONTENT into one number is reporting two different facts under the louder one's name — and when the provenance term is derived from the tree's own HEAD, the check is not flaky, it is unsatisfiable. When an instrument compares a pinned artifact to a live derivation, ask which of its fields can EVER agree, and refuse to let a field that structurally cannot agree set the exit code.**

