e-abridged-declaration-guard.test.mjs` — 11 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`, `gate-caller-audit` PASS.** 🔬 **TEETH, 9 variants on scratch copies with the subject restored byte-identical AND THE RESTORATION ASSERTED (sha `6f1138526c04` both sides); per s2226's duty the sweep doubled as a reachability audit and **every one of the 11 arms reds under at least one variant**, so none is decoration. Each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it: PRE-CURE verbatim reds `2,3,4,8,9,10,11` · *always say nothing was lost* (the tempting cure, since the live case was benign) reds **arm 3** · *leaking the declaration into `--quiet`* reds **arm 7 ALONE** · *letting an abridgement red the exit code* reds **arm 6 ALONE** · *reclassifying as superseded* reds `1,2,4,5,7,10,11`.** ⚠️ **TWO METHOD NOTES PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE, both caught by controls rather than by reading. (1) MY FIRST FIXTURE NEVER REACHED THE ARM: I built the "extension" as a pure APPEND, which leaves the older line WHOLLY CONTAINED in the child, so the audit short-circuits at *"properly archived, verbatim"* and `abridged` stays `0`. The live case inserts MID-LINE (s2586 raised a desk count `4 → 7`), which is what breaks containment — the fixture now ASSERTS its own shape before any arm reads it. (2) MY FIRST TEETH SWEEP SCORED ONE VARIANT AS A CONSTRUCTION REFUSAL, correctly: its two-line anchor no longer matched because MY OWN comment block now sits between the two lines. Arm 7 had teeth from a different variant, so it looked covered — but **an arm named for a defence it cannot provide is worse than no arm** (the s2491 lesson), so the anchor was re-derived by grep and arm 7 now reds for its own reason.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS: this streak has spent thirty fires asking how a SUBJECT SET can be wrong — too narrow, wrong tree, wrong axis, a registry not a census, entries not files, no durability predicate. Here the subject set is perfect and the CLASSIFICATION IS CORRECT;