🧾 **F-2586-1 — THE §2E EVIDENCE SWEEP'S *UNTRACKED* HALF HAD NO INSTRUMENT, SO NINE FIRES REBUILT IT FROM PROSE AND SIX OF THEM SHIPPED A DEFECT IN THEIR OWN VERIFIER (measured and cured s2586).** `modified-tracked-evidence-census.mjs` (s2585) computes the MODIFIED-TRACKED half and **declares in its own output that "the untracked half is F-2357-1"** — a duty on EVERY dry board, with no command. 📊 **THE HAND-REBUILD ERROR RATE IS MEASURED, NOT FEARED: s2560 · s2570 · s2571 · s2572 · s2581 · s2582 · s2584 · s2585 · s2586 each rebuilt it, and SIX found a defect in their own hand-built verifier — F-2570-1 (the bucket LABEL), F-2571-1 (the cure scoped one bucket too narrow), F-2572-1 (the verifier's OWN KEYS — a transform relocates the path and a retention ref is named for the fire that minted it), F-2581-1 (an entry has TWO shapes; a `parts[]`-only test scores a whole-stored file `0/0`), F-2582-1 (presence is not recoverability).** 🛠️ **CURE: `node scripts/untracked-evidence-durability.mjs` — four buckets always printed (F-2560-1) with F-2566-1's prunable-fuse correction at the site, the retention-transform test on EVERY non-SAFE bucket (F-2571-1) resolving `parts[]` **or** `storedAs` (F-2581-1) BY PATH in the holding ref's tree and REFUSING an ambiguous suffix rather than guessing (F-2572-1), `--verify-bytes` streaming every part against the manifest's own sha256 (F-2582-1), F-2495-1's in-flight test by epoch-ms on both sides (F-2567-1), controls asserted before any zero is believed (F-2215-1), `--all-trees` for the whole registry (F-2488-1/F-2489-1), and `2` = could-not-answer vs `1` = FACTORY-SIDE bytes at risk — attended-owned never reds (F-1460-1/F-2561-1).** ✅ **IT REPRODUCES EVERY BANKED FIGURE, which is the regression test F-2581-1 says a banked count buys, and it PRINTS them so a successor gets it free: main tree `AT RISK 0 · UNREFERENCED 2 · LOCAL-REF-ONLY 4 · SAFE 91`, `6/6` preserved, `23/23` parts origin-reachable, and — first time for this arm — `6/6` RECONSTRUCT to the manifest's own sha256 under `--verify-bytes`.** 🪞 **AND IT NEARLY SHIPPED THE VERY AMBIGUITY IT CITES, WHICH IS THE HALF WORTH CARRYING: my `--all-trees` run printed `AT RISK 554`, and that number is the **UNION** of the F-2569-2 desk figure (`516`, modified-tracked) and the untracked at-risk — two populations under one heading, on a figure that is read onto an OWNER decision row. That is F-2585-1 one population over, reproduced by the fire citing it. **CURED: AT RISK now splits by POPULATION, in the human output and in `--json`, and says which half is the desk figure and which is not.** ➡️ **So when you give a count a name, ask whether its SUBJECT SET is one population or two — a union wearing a single label is a figure with two readings, and F-2585-1's cure (put the command beside the figure) does not help if the command answers a wider question than the row.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/untracked-evidence-durability-guard.test.mjs` — 19 arms, 5.6 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; `gate-caller-audit` PASS. The fixture carries a REAL origin, because F-2560-1 records that a fixture WITHOUT one measures a different question (every committed asset is legitimately LOCAL-REF-ONLY and that bucket appears to discriminate for the wrong reason).** 🔬 **TEETH, 19 variants on scratch copies with the subject restored byte-identical and the restoration ASSERTED: decoration count **0** — but only after the sweep caught TWO of my own defects, which is why the sweep is worth more than the tool. (1) MY `--verify-bytes` ARM PASSED ON THE WRONG CHECK: the manufactured corruption was SHORTER than the original, so the BYTE-COUNT check caught it and deleting the sha256 check reddened NOTHING. The corruption is now byte-length-identical by construction and the arm asserts `sha256 mismatch` specifically and `doesNotMatch` byte mismatch — F-2582-1's own lesson landing on the TEST instead of the tool. (2) SEVEN ARMS WERE REDDENED BY NO VARIANT on the first pass, i.e. candidate decoration, and seven more variants had to be built before every arm was covered.** ⚠️ **ONE HARNESS BLIND SPOT RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN, and it is s2585's own, reproduced: the `ignores --root` variant is caught LOUDLY (`rc=null`, killed on its 240 s bound, because anchoring to its own directory makes every fixture arm sweep the REAL 127-tree board) but reds no NAMED arm, so my parser scored it as covering nothing. A reachability audit is itself an instrument, and its inability to name an arm is indistinguishable from the absence of coverage it exists to find. That arm is covered by a different variant, so the verdict stands.** 💰 **COST, with its load condition stated because a scalar cost is a measurement with a hidden parameter (F-2452-1): main tree `~60 s` on a quiet board; `--all-trees` is `~10 min` and reads ~120 GB (it hashes 99,205 subjects), so it is a FIRE-scope act and NOT a gate-scope one — the guard runs on fixtures via `--root` in 5.6 s. `--verify-bytes` streams `743 MB`.** 🚫 **NO BOARD GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: an untracked file in a live tree is a LAWFUL routine state, so a red would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — the restraint F-2357-1 through F-2582-1 all took for this very sweep. What IS guarded is our own verifier.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is this factory's most-repeated finding on a NEW axis: the eleven before it are cures with no reader, or alarms with no remedy. THIS ONE IS A DUTY WITH NO INSTRUMENT, WHOSE SIBLING HALF HAS ONE AND SAYS SO IN ITS OWN OUTPUT. When a tool declares a boundary, read the declaration as a WORK ITEM and not as a disclaimer — `the untracked half is F-2357-1` named the gap for 1 fire and nobody heard it as an assignment.**

📌 **F-2585-1 — THE F-2569-2 DESK ROW STATES A *FIGURE* AND NAMES NO *PREDICATE* AND NO *INSTRUMENT*, AND ITS TWO PLAUSIBLE READINGS DIFFER ~3× (measured s2585).** The row reads *"`516` modified-tracked evidence files / `496.5 MB` sit AT RISK in `26` ATTENDED-OWNED trees"* and gives the next reader no way to re-derive it. That matters because re-derivation is the NORM for this row, not an edge case — its own text records `421` → `431` → `516` across five fires — and the four-bucket durability predicate this factory teaches (F-2560-1/F-2560-2) has THREE non-SAFE buckets, so "AT RISK" has a narrow reading and a wide one. 📊 **MEASURED s2585 over all `126` registered worktrees, controls asserted first (F-2215-1: `35,176` tracked · `122,567` remote-reachable · `184,597` all-ref-reachable · hash-count-equals-subject-count, so a zero is an ANSWER): the NARROW reading (in NO object database) is **`516` files / `496.5 MB` / `26` trees**; the WIDE reading (AT RISK + UNREFERENCED + LOCAL-REF-ONLY) is **`1,569` files / `1,853.8 MB` / `28` trees`** — 3.0× the files, 3.7× the bytes, and two extra trees.** ⓘ **The gap is almost entirely ONE attended tree: `~/.codex/worktrees/5b60/Gold Rush` contributes `1,041` files / `1,348.1 MB` that are in the object database but on no origin ref — correctly EXCLUDED by the narrow reading, and dominant under the wide one.** ✅ **AND THE DESK FIGURE IS CONFIRMED CURRENT, re-measured independently this fire rather than inherited: `516` / `496.5 MB` / `26` trees, UNCHANGED from s2584, same four largest trees in the same order, still **100% attended-owned and ZERO factory-side**. The AT RISK bucket was also verified to be `516/516` MODIFIED-TRACKED and `0` untracked, so the row's LABEL is right as well as its number.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED — THIS IS A NEAR-MISS, NOT A REALISED HARM: realised cost ZERO, nothing is broken, no verdict anywhere was wrong, and this is NOT a false green. **Measured recurrence: `0` of the `5` prior re-measurements got it wrong** — s2569, s2576, s2578, s2582 and s2584 all used the narrow reading. The one data point on the other side is MINE: my own registry sweep computed the wide reading first, and I would have published `1,569` onto an owner decision row had I not measured both and noticed they disagreed.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is WHO READS IT and WHAT TURNS ON IT: the desk is the owner's decision queue, and this row's RECOMMENDATION is SIZED off the denominator (*"salvage ~198 files, ~250 MB"* is a percentage of it). A 3× inflation does not merely misreport the pile, it re-prices the decision the owner is being asked to make — and the row already carries a warning that its `~45%/~49%` split is stale, so the next fire to touch it is EXPECTED to re-measure.** 🛠️ **CURE — the row now names both, and the instrument exists: `node scripts/modified-tracked-evidence-census.mjs`.** It sweeps every registered worktree (inside the root as well as outside, F-2489-1), takes the modified-tracked population only, classifies against all four buckets, and **PRINTS ALL FOUR plus an explicit `➡️ THE DESK FIGURE is the AT RISK bucket` line naming the wide reading as NOT the desk figure** — so the predicate is visible at the call site and cannot be swapped silently. Corpus declared on stdout ALWAYS including the happy path (F-2208-1); `2` = could-not-answer separated from `1` = answered-and-refuses; a tree that cannot answer is counted, never treated as empty (F-2485-1). 🚦 **`--strict` reds ONLY on FACTORY-SIDE at-risk bytes, and that restraint is MEASURED rather than stylistic: attended-owned at-risk is the NORMAL state here (`516` of `516` today) and is an OWNER call a fire must not touch (F-2561-1), so a red on it would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate). The tool answers the ACTIONABLE question — *is any of this MINE to fix?* — and today the answer is `0`.** 🚫 **NO GUARD over the prose row itself, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: *"does this row name its predicate?"* is a JUDGEMENT, so a red would fire on every honest desk row — the same restraint F-2450-1 took for a live instruction and F-2492-1 for an expired convention.** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/modified-tracked-evidence-census-guard.test.mjs` — 15 arms, 3.3 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`; `gate-caller-audit` PASS.** 🔬 **TEETH, 12 variants manufactured on scratch copies with the subject restored byte-identical and the restoration ASSERTED by sha256: every substantive arm reds under at least one variant, and each over-general cure is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it — swapping the desk figure to the wide union reds arms 1/3, `-uno`→`-uall` reds arm 3, dropping the prefix filter reds arm 4, declaring only on failure reds arm 6, **`--strict` reddening on ANY at-risk (the over-general cure) reds arm 7b ALONE**, and `isFactorySide` keyed on a path SUFFIX reds arm 9 ALONE.** ⚠️ **THREE METHOD NOTES PAID FOR IN THIS FIRE, AND THE FIRST IS WORTH MORE THAN THE CURE. (1) MY GUARD'S FIRST FIXTURES WERE VACUOUS AND THE TELL WAS A TIMEOUT, NOT A FAILED ASSERTION: the subject is ANCHORED to its own directory on purpose (F-2221-1), so a fixture that only sets `cwd` measures the REAL repo — every arm still passed, about the wrong subject, until the `-uall` variant swept 97k files and died on its 240 s bound. The cure was an explicit `--root`, and F-2215-1's rule needed sharpening to match: assert not merely that the control PRODUCED something, but that it produced something ABOUT THE RIGHT SUBJECT — the CONTROL arm now asserts `treesRegistered === 1`, because the live board has 126. (2) THE REACHABILITY SWEEP FOUND THREE ARMS THAT ASSERTED NOTHING — arms 1, 4 and 7 were DECORATION on the first pass, each because its fixture made its own defect invisible: arm 1's fixture had no UNREFERENCED file, so the narrow and wide readings COINCIDED and the swap was un