✅ **F-2576-2 (CURED s2577 by F-2577-1 — the restraint below was CORRECT about the cure it names, and a DIFFERENT route needed none of it; see F-2577-1) — `status-archive-audit`’S SAME-SESSION-REWRITE EXCLUSION IS KEYED ON AN `sNNNN` TOKEN, SO IT CAN NEVER FIRE FOR AN *ATTENDED* LINE — AND EVERY ATTENDED SELF-UPDATE THEREFORE REPORTS AS A DESTROYED HANDOFF (measured s2576).** The audit already HAS the right idea and says so in its own summary (*"6 same-session rewrites excluded"*) — a fire that rewrites its own line-1 is not destroying anyone’s work. **But it identifies a session by the `sNNNN` token in the line, and an ATTENDED line carries none**, so both sides of an attended self-update parse to the same null value and the comparison still reads as a cross-session destruction. 🔑 **THE TELL IS PRINTED IN THE OUTPUT AND IS UNMISTAKABLE ONCE YOU LOOK AT IT: `snull destroyed snull’s handoff line`. Both sides are the SAME parsed value. An exclusion for "same session" is looking straight at two equal session ids and not firing.** 📊 **MEASURED s2576 on the live instance: `8aa8a5b9` is flagged as destroying a 1,517-char handoff line. Its parent’s line-1 and its own are the SAME attended handoff — diffed rather than assumed, identical for the first 282 characters, diverging at exactly the point where the older reads *"deploy follows this handoff"* and the newer reads *"DEPLOYED + VERIFIED `0cc9fe38` at 05:20Z (first attempt: transient Cloudflare fetch failure, nothing published; retry green)"*. The attended session wrote a handoff, performed the deploy, and updated its own line to record the result. The newer line is 1,628 chars and strictly SUPERSEDES the older.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING WAS LOST, nothing is broken, and this is NOT a false green — it is a FALSE RED, an alarm louder than the truth, the same class as F-2566-1 and F-2570-1.**
🎯 **What earns it a row is that the red is in the MANDATED closing battery and it PERSISTS: `test:ledger-guards` exits 1 on it, every fire from here will inherit it, and the honest report is "the battery did not come back clean". A red that fires on ordinary correct attended behaviour is exactly the thing that gets excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — and once excused, it stops protecting the case it exists for, which is a REAL destroyed line-1 (F-2403-1, priced at a whole handoff going unarchived).** 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT CURED, AND THE RESTRAINT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN LAZY — THE OBVIOUS FIX IS THE DANGEROUS ONE: treating "both sides parse to null" as "same session" would collapse EVERY attended line into one identity, so two genuinely different attended sessions on the same day would also be excluded, and a real attended-side destruction would go unreported. That is the exact loss this instrument exists to catch, so the over-general cure trades a false RED for a false GREEN — the wrong direction. A sound fix needs a session identity an attended line actually carries (its own commit, or a stamp) plus behaviour-neutrality proof and a teeth sweep; that is a task, not a drive-by, and re-coding a working instrument in passing is what this factory calls a drive-by.** ➡️ **UNTIL THEN, FOR THE NEXT FIRE READING A RED BATTERY: if the only failure is `status-archive-audit` naming `snull destroyed snull`, DIFF THE TWO LINES before believing it — `git show <parent>:STATUS.md` against `git show <sha>:STATUS.md`, first line each. If they are the same handoff restamped or updated, it is this finding and nothing is owed. If they differ in SUBSTANCE, it is F-2403-1 and you owe the recovery.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the mirror of F-2576-1 filed beside it: that one is a loss no instrument reports; this one is a report with no loss. Both come from the same root — **an instrument that identifies actors by a token only SOME actors carry**. The fire side of this factory is `sNNNN`-shaped and the attended side is not, so every guard keyed on that token silently has two populations and has only ever been tested on one.**

✏️ **F-2578-1 — THE WEEKLY-BUDGET COUNTER'S `uncited` BLIND SPOT IS JUSTIFIED BY A CLAIM THAT IS 76% FALSE — AND THE CURE IT INVITES IS *MEASURED WORTHLESS AND NAIVELY HARMFUL*, SO THE FINDING IS THE NEGATIVE (measured s2578).** F-2491-1 landed the weekly headline counter precisely because the ≤3/week rule is an aggregate no single fire can see. It dates each item by its `merge:` token and drops every item carrying none into an `uncited` bucket **counted in NO week** — honestly PRINTED (`counted in NO week: 117 item(s)`), and justified in the code as *"the pre-2026-08 house format"*. 📊 **THAT JUSTIFICATION IS MEASURABLY FALSE: of the 117, `27` were filed in 2026-07 and **`89` on or after 2026-08-01** (1 undatable) — 76% of the hole is not the old format at all.** ⛔ **BUT DO NOT BUILD THE FALLBACK IT INVITES. I BUILT IT, PRICED IT, AND IT CHANGES NOTHING.** An item's FILING date — the queue commit that first adds its `## ` line — is a sound substitute, agreeing with merge-week on **214 of 216** datable items (**99.1%**); the 2 divergences are backfills and **both are already ROUNDUP-batched**, so they spend no slot under either reading. ⚙️ **THE MECHANISM IS WHY, AND IT IS SELF-REINFORCING: fires file their GZ-01 item AT DRAIN TIME, so filing-week ≡ merge-week BY CONSTRUCTION, and the only way to break that is a BACKFILL — which the ≤3/week batching rule itself forces into a ROUNDUP. The rule's own discipline keeps its instrument's two possible clocks aligned.** 📐 **PRICED PER WEEK, all three readings side by side: adding the fallback flips the over/under-budget verdict for **0 of 11 weeks**. W28–W36 are already over by 4–13× (13–40 standalone against a budget of 3) and W37/W38 sit at exactly `3 standalone, 2 batched` and contain **no uncited items at all**.** 🚨 **AND THE NAIVE FORM IS ACTIVELY WORSE, WHICH IS THE REVERSE CONTROL: `29` of the uncited paragraphs are DISMISSALS (`## SWEEP NOTE …` / `NOT PLAYER-VISIBLE`), and `isBatchedItem` matches only `ROUNDUP-CLASS`/`## ROUNDUP` — so dating them scores all 29 as STANDALONE headlines, **+10 phantom in W33 and +15 in W34**, pushing fires to batch news that needed no batching. A cure aimed at an under-count would have manufactured an over-count.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, NOT a false green, nothing is broken, and no verdict anywhere was wrong — the tool reports the hole's SIZE correctly on every run; only its stated CAUSE was wrong. The hole is also currently EMPTY: **zero** uncited items have been filed since 2026-09-01, because every fire now cites its merge.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is that the false cause is the half a reader ACTS on: a fire seeing *"pre-2026-08 house format"* concludes the hole is closed legacy and stops looking, when 89 of its members are recent — and the direction of an under-count is toward filing a standalone headline that should have been batched, the exact harm F-2491-1 exists to prevent.** 🛠️ **CURED AS A COMMENT AT THE SITE, not as code: the false claim is replaced by the measured figures, the fallback's 99.1% agreement, the 0-of-11 flip count and the 29-dismissal reverse control — so the next fire inherits the PRICE of this cure rather than the temptation. Comment-only; the sweep's output is byte-identical (138 lines, `reported 256 / dismissed 118 / candidates 0`) before and after.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: the subject is a code COMMENT's accuracy, which no battery can observe, and the same reason F-2414-1 declined a guard for a cited count that is MEANT to move (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate). The cure is the comment you are reading.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS after *how WIDE is the selector* (F-2358-1), *can its axis EXPRESS the defect* (F-2389-1) and *how many subjects did the author VISIT* (F-2487-1): **A DECLARED BLIND SPOT CARRIES A SIZE AND A STORY, AND ONLY THE SIZE IS MEASURED.** F-2208-1 taught this factory to make instruments