✏️ **F-2569-1 — EVERY SELECTOR IN THE §2E EVIDENCE SWEEP IS `--others`, i.e. UNTRACKED; A TRACKED FILE MODIFIED IN PLACE IS AT RISK BY THE SAME MECHANISM AND IS INVISIBLE TO ALL TEN FINDINGS IN THE CHAIN.** The anchor is F-2358-1 itself: it taught this streak to *"enumerate every key your cure selects on"*, listed three — LOCATION, TRACKED-NESS, IGNORE STATUS — and marked the second **"(`--others`, correct)"** in passing. LOCATION was questioned twice (F-2358-1 widened it, F-2389-1 abolished it) and IGNORE STATUS once; **TRACKED-NESS was certified in a parenthesis and never revisited, by eleven consecutive fires.** 📊 MEASURED s2569 over the WHOLE registry (F-2488-1’s duty — `120` registered, `102` answered, `18` could-not-answer, the known prunable set), each read’s CONTROL asserted first (F-2215-1 — `121,566` remote objects; hashed-count == file-count per tree): `1,591` modified-tracked files fleet-wide, `1,539` under an evidence prefix, across `28` trees — **AT RISK `444` · UNREFERENCED `1,059` · SAFE `36`**, totalling **`483.5 MB`** at risk. 🕳️ The blindness is TOTAL: in `worktrees/lane-d` the prescribed `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` returns **`0`** while `26` tracked files carry disk bytes matching NEITHER main NOR the lane’s own HEAD (`29,939` tracked files asserted present in the same breath, so the zero is a real answer). ⚖️ **SEVERITY HONEST AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED, AND THE OBVIOUS HEADLINE IS THE WRONG ONE: realised cost ZERO, nothing lost, and this is NOT "444 files of lost work" — every path is TRACKED, so a committed version exists and is safe; only the NEWER on-disk render is undurable.** I tested the churn hypothesis rather than assuming (F-2182-1): the class is **HETEROGENEOUS** — `17` differ in PNG DIMENSIONS (a real re-shoot, 1000x625 → 1280x800), `181` same dims with ≥2% byte delta (real visual delta), `218` same dims within 2% (CHURN-LIKE), `28` not comparable. **~45% plausibly real, ~49% plausibly noise; byte-difference alone does not discriminate.** 🎯 What earns it a clause: **the instruments are INVERTED relative to the law’s own value ordering** — §2E says *"only tracked dirt can be someone’s unsaved work"*, and the sweep built seven judging tests plus a four-bucket durability predicate for the population the law calls DEBRIS and none for the one it calls WORK. ⚙️ The fuse is SHARED and is CODE: `lane-runner-v3.sh:550` runs `git reset --hard main && git clean -fd` — `clean -fd` kills the untracked half, **`reset --hard` kills the modified-tracked half**. ✅ MITIGATIONS, so this is not over-read: lane-d is protected TODAY by `lane-usable`’s `DIRTY` (rc 2 = do not refill), and §2E is suspended outright by the standing owner CODEX-WALL — latent, not live. ➡️ **CURE (landed in `scripts/fire.md` §2E): take the read a second time with `git status --porcelain -uno` in every registered tree and put it through F-2560-1’s SAME durability predicate — identical two processes, only the selector changes.** 🔑 SALVAGED s2569, factory-side trees ONLY (`worktrees/lane-d` 17 + `gate-s2501` 6 + 6 UNREFERENCED siblings = `29` files / `32.7 MB`) to `save/modified-tracked-evidence-s2569` = `3261e92bc`, PARENTLESS, built through a throwaway `GIT_INDEX_FILE`; untouchedness MEASURED not trusted (before/after `git status --porcelain -uall` identical at `157/26/9`); PUSHED and re-verified **`30 of 30` origin-reachable** (F-1055-1). Both factory trees now re-measure **AT RISK 0 · UNREFERENCED 0**. 🚫 NO GUARD — a modified tracked file in a live tree is a LAWFUL routine state, so a red fires on ordinary correct operation and is excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1); the same restraint F-2357-1, F-2389-1, F-2484-1, F-2485-1, F-2487-1, F-2488-1, F-2489-1 and F-2495-1 all took for this sweep. 💡 **REUSABLE, a NEW AXIS: every prior rung interrogates a selector the author CHOSE. This one was never chosen — it was inherited from the first `git ls-files --others` anyone typed, certified in a parenthesis, and carried by ten findings that each believed they were questioning everything. When you audit a cure’s selectors, the dangerous one is not the one under discussion — it is the one already marked "correct".**

🔺 **F-2569-2 — OWNER CALL: `516` modified-tracked evidence files / `496.5 MB` sit AT RISK in `26` ATTENDED-OWNED trees. Salvage them, or let them go?** ⏱️ **FIGURE RE-MEASURED s2584 — was `421` / `~451 MB` (s2569) and `431` / `469.3 MB` (s2576), RESTATED NOT DELETED because the SEQUENCE is the content: the TREE COUNT is unchanged at `26` across all three readings while the file count grew `421 → 431 → 516` (+22.6%) and the bytes `451 → 469.3 → 496.5 MB` (+10.1%), and the four largest trees are the SAME four in the same order — so this is one population ACCRETING, not a new one, and the row ages by roughly `+6 files/fire` while it waits.** Priced rather than acted on, per the F-2563-1 precedent that *a one-word remedy with an unstated magnitude is discovered by attempting it*. The trees are `.claude/worktrees/agent-*` (14), `gr-task-*` (7), `~/.codex/worktrees/*` (1) and attended scratchpads (2) — **NOT a fire’s to touch (F-2561-1), which is why s2569 salvaged only its own two and stopped.** Largest (s2584, by bytes): `gr-task-beauty-dry-gulch` 58 files / 71.6 MB · `agent-aa7ccb79d2d03ada8` 44 / 57.3 MB · `agent-a6b1bbd373315d0c0` 50 / 49.7 MB · `agent-a074ca5aabe748fbe` 45 / 45.2 MB (was 68.3 / 47.4 / 43.1 / 54.6 MB at s2569 — same four trees, same order by file count). ⚖️ **The honest case for LEAVING them is strong and is stated first: every path is TRACKED so a committed version already exists, ~49% of the class is churn-like (same PNG dimensions, <2% byte delta) that nobody wants in git, and the RETENTION LAW’s own owner amendment of 2026-08-26 (*"keep the run logs local for now"*) already exempted a 2.4 GB evidence class from the mirror-into-git half.** The case for salvaging is the RETENTION LAW’s core (Mistake #11, the thing that dies with the disk) and that ~45% shows a real content delta. ➡️ **RECOMMENDATION: salvage the DIMENSION-CHANGE and ≥2% classes only (~198 files, ~`250 MB` est.) to a parentless `save/*` ref and push; let the churn go.** ⚠️ **THAT SP