🔁 **F-2568-1 — A DUTY AND THE GATE THAT GUARDS ITS OUTPUT ARE JOINTLY UNSATISFIABLE, AND THE ONLY THING PROTECTING THE FACTORY IS THAT THE DUTY HAS ALWAYS RUN LATE.** RT-01 orders the minting fire to set `CURRENT_ROTATION_ID` to *"the rotation that is OPEN (not the one just minted)"*, and triggers on *"the first fire after Sunday 00:00 UTC"* for a rotation whose `opensAt` is **the coming Monday** — so at an on-time mint the new rotation has NOT opened. `scripts/skillmd-guard.test.mjs:103` (cite the CODE, the coordinate drifts) asserts `CURRENT_ROTATION_ID` equals `rotations.rotations.at(-1).id`, the newest MINTED (`rotation-mint.mjs:53` sorts by `opensAt`, so `at(-1)` always opens last). **The law says OPEN; the gate says NEWEST; on the Sunday those differ.** 📊 **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING, predicate DERIVED from the guard’s own source line rather than transcribed, live tree asserted as a passing CONTROL first (F-2215-1): on-time mint of `r2026w39` at Sunday 2026-09-20T07:00Z — obey RT-01 (`CURRENT=‘r2026w38’`) → **guard RED**; obey the gate (`CURRENT=‘r2026w39’`) → **GREEN, and the public board points at an unopened rotation.** REVERSE CONTROL, a LATE mint after `opensAt`: they **AGREE**.** ⚙️ **WHY IT HAS NEVER FIRED, and both escapes are accidents: the only real mint `66b782b09` landed 2026-09-14T04:21Z against `opensAt` 00:00Z — `4h22m` LATE, so `at(-1)` WAS the open one; `r2026w37` was the bootstrap with no predecessor.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY HONEST AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing broken, no verdict anywhere wrong, NOT a false green — a guard red is LOUD.** 🎯 **DIRECTION earns it, with a DATED trigger: `skillmd-guard` is a leg of `test:node-guards`, a mandated gate, so a fire obeying RT-01 ON TIME gets a red and the obvious "fix" points the family’s browser at a rotation that has not opened. Next mint `r2026w39`, trigger Sunday **2026-09-20**; fires run every 5 min, so an on-time mint is the DEFAULT outcome.** ➡️ **CURED AT THE SITE in `scripts/fire.md` RT-01 (F-2436-1’s duty applied to a sentence), BINDING until the owner rules: mint ON OR AFTER the Monday `opensAt` — the only jointly-satisfiable window, and what the working practice already does — never on the Sunday; and NEVER clear a red `skillmd-guard` by moving `CURRENT_ROTATION_ID` onto a rotation whose `opensAt` is in the future.** ⓘ **Tradeoff NAMED not hidden: between Monday 00:00Z and the mint the constant still names the just-CLOSED rotation, and `functions/api/standings.ts:492–493` accepts any listed rotation with **no window check**. Bounded by fire cadence (~5 min) vs the Sunday mint’s guaranteed 24 h.** 🚫 **NO GUARD CHANGE, restraint measured: a time-aware pin would red through every lawful Sunday→Monday window and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate); abolishing the constant is a player-facing `site/` change while the CODEX-WALL suspends §2E authoring. ⇒ **F-2568-2 ON THE DESK.** 💡 **REUSABLE, a NEW AXIS: twenty-odd findings asked how a MEASUREMENT can be wrong — a swallow, a guard, a cwd, a filename, a timezone, a clock. THIS IS A DUTY AND A GATE EACH INDIVIDUALLY CORRECT THAT CANNOT BOTH BE OBEYED. Neither is a defect alone; the defect is the PAIR, and no instrument here examines pairs. When a duty writes a value a gate pins, ask whether the duty’s SCHEDULE can put them out of agreement — and if the only evidence they agree is that the duty always ran late, you are being protected by an accident.**

