⏰ **F-2567-1 — A DERIVED "N DAYS QUIET" IS A MEASUREMENT WITH A HIDDEN CLOCK, AND A FIRE HOLDS TWO CLOCKS THAT DISAGREE BY SEVEN HOURS.** F-2495-1’s sixth judging test prescribes *"one `stat` for the tree’s newest mtime BEFORE you judge"* and is SILENT on the other half of the subtraction. A fire’s nearest "now" is its own §1.3 stamp — LOCAL time wearing a `Z` (Bangkok, UTC+07; re-verified s2567 by direct observation: `date "+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ"` printed `23:14Z` while true UTC was `16:18`) — while an mtime read through `mtimeMs`/`toISOString()` is TRUE UTC, so mixing them inflates every quiet reading by exactly **+7h**. 📊 MEASURED on the standing sweep’s own subject `artifacts/deploy-budget-production-probe/` (newest mtime `2026-09-05T05:37:05.723Z`, UNMOVED across three fires): s2565 reported `9.3` days quiet, s2566 reported `9.7`, s2567 measures `9.45` from the epoch. 🔑 **THE TELL NEEDS NO TIMEZONE KNOWLEDGE: 63 minutes separated those two handoffs and the reported age grew by 0.4 days — an age that ages faster than the clock.** The mechanism reconstructs to 0.01 d (stamp-as-LOCAL → `9.35`/`9.40`; stamp-as-UTC → `9.64`/`9.69`) but is labelled an INFERENCE per F-2182-1; the divergence itself is measured. ⚖️ **SEVERITY HONEST AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, NOT a false green, no verdict anywhere was wrong** — F-2565-1’s banked expiry condition is *"has the mtime MOVED"*, an unchanged string compared against itself, so all three fires agreed and all three were right. 🎯 **DIRECTION is what earns it: the skew always makes a subject look MORE FINISHED than it is** (a tree written 3 h ago reads as 10 h quiet), flipping F-2495-1 off its safe arm (*"Still being written ⇒ REPORT, DO NOT TOUCH"*) onto its acting arm — whose end point that clause itself names as a fire reaching into a live lane or arena, the Mistake #2 direction. Reachable on any ordinary day: an attended heat writes continuously and fires run every five minutes. ➡️ **CURE, landed at the site