🔺 **F-1458-2 (s1458, MEASURED — THE RUNNER CERTIFIES WORK ON AN OFF-PIN INTERPRETER, SO ITS GREENS ARE NOT EVIDENCE FOR THE ENVIRONMENT EVERY FIRE GATES IN. OWNER QUESTION.)** The ER-01 runner reported its new spec **8/8 green and was telling the truth about its own shell.** `.nvmrc` pins **26.4.0** (repo root AND `worktrees/lane-b`); the Codex binary that executed this run lives at `/Users/robin/.nvm/versions/node/v23.11.1/…` — **verified for THIS run from its own run log, not inherited from F-1404-2.** Measured side by side, same code, same machine: **v23.11.1 reading `globalThis.localStorage` → stderr EMPTY · v26.4.0 → ExperimentalWarning.** F-1403-1/F-1404-2 already found this split for a cross-V8 `Math.pow` HASH divergence and treated it as exotic, with a documented skip mechanism. **This finding shows the same split produces ORDINARY, EVERYDAY REDS**: any spec asserting on console output is exposed, the runner structurally cannot see it, and the fire discovers it only at drain time. It is F-1457-1 one turn further out — not *a fire can pick the wrong instrument*, but **the two halves of the factory routinely run DIFFERENT instruments and only one matches the pin.** ➡️ **RECOMMENDATION (owner/attended, not fire-decidable): either align the runner onto `.nvmrc`, or declare 23.11.1 the runner supported engine and gate that claim.** Until one lands, every console-asserting spec is a latent drain refusal. **GATE: an owner/attended word.**

