- 🔎 **F-2259-1 `desk-birth-guard` CLAIMS "EVERY OWNER-GATED ROW FILED THIS WINDOW REACHED THE DESK" OVER A CORPUS ITS PARSER SILENTLY NARROWS (s2259, NON-BLOCKING, CURED SAME FIRE).** The PASS ranges over whatever `addedRows()` admitted, and that parser takes a line only if it **LEADS** with one of four glyphs after whitespace, or contains the literal `**F-`. A row contributing to neither cannot enter `qualifying`, so it is **structurally incapable of failing the gate** — F-2256-1's shape one file over, in the sibling guard, one fire later. 🔑 **WHY IT SURVIVED: THE TWO ADMISSION TESTS EACH COVER THE OTHER'S BLIND SPOT, so a row escapes ONLY when it uses BOTH house conventions AT ONCE** — a markdown bullet before the glyph **and** the bracketed `**[F-id]` key. Measured: `🔺 **F-9999-1**` admitted (glyph) · `- 🔺 **F-9999-1**` admitted (`**F-`) · `🔺 **[F-9999-1]` admitted (glyph) · `- 🔺 **[F-9999-1]` **ESCAPED**. Neither convention is exotic — the live BACKLOG carries **353** bullet-then-glyph rows, **47** bracketed keys and **38** lines in the escaping shape today; glyphs outside the admitted four (🔵, 👑, 🟢) escape outright. 📐 **THE FILE PRICED THE WRONG TWO THINGS, AND ITS OWN HEADER SHOWS IT:** the 2×2 table at the top prices the SELECTOR (which gates count) against MEMBERSHIP (what the desk carries), over 25 windows and 96 rows — and never prices the CORPUS both range over. 📊 **MEASURED over all 2,459 BACKLOG-touching commits: 10 owner-gated keyed rows escaped, of which 5 are REAL owner items** — `F-1637-2` and `F-1625-4` (**BOTH ON ROBIN'S DESK TODAY**), `F-1617-1`, `F-BT-2` (🔵) and `F-1118-2` (👑); the declaration is non-zero in **15** real handoff windows. ⚖️ **SEVERITY, HONESTLY AND NOT INFLATED: LATENT.** Replaying all **1,133** real handoff windows, every one of those rows had already been desked by hand in the same handoff, so the blindness has never actually cost a desk entry. What it costs is the guarantee: the PASS cannot mean what it says. 🚦 **CURED BY DECL