ts correctness): the remedy says put the id on the OWNER'S DESK, so obeying a false red MANUFACTURES owner-desk items out of completion rows, onto a desk already carrying 27.** 🚦 **CURED BY DECLARATION, AND THE RESTRAINT IS THE DESIGN (F-2218-1, F-2225-1): `ownerGateDecidedAt()` reports WHERE the admission was decided; `analyse()` carries it on every qualifying row; the FAIL output names the offset and flags anything past the measured p95 of 162 as the false-positive shape. MEMBERSHIP IS UNCHANGED.** ⛔ **BOUNDING `gateOf()` OR DROPPING FAR-DECIDED ROWS WAS CONSIDERED AND DECLINED ON MEASURE: it is the PERMISSIVE direction in a guard whose entire purpose is that "an owner fork on no desk is on no board Robin reads" — a false RED is waived in one line, a false GREEN is silent forever — and a cutoff drawn on a population of 69 is exactly the GUESSED boundary F-2206-1 forbids.** ✅ **BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL BEFORE LANDING (F-1274-2): driven against the pre-cure blob over all 2,022 live rows — `69` qualifying and `69` missing on BOTH sides with IDENTICAL id sequences, the control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1: *"pre-cure kind=window qualifying=69 — it really ran"*).** 🔒 **Guarded by `scripts/desk-birth-gate-distance-guard.test.mjs` — 10 arms, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`.** 🔬 **TEETH, every variant manufactured on the real file with an in-memory restore in `finally` (s2247: never `git checkout` a file you are editing): PRE-CURE reds 8 of 10 · FLATTENING the offset to a boolean reds 4 · FARTHEST-instead-of-NEAREST reds 1 · dropping negation handling reds 2 including the live-ledger agreement invariant · SEAM-SEVERED reds 1 · and **each of the two cures I declined is caught by exactly the reverse control built for it — the `> 162` cutoff reds the far-row arm ALONE, the inverted cutoff reds the near-row arm.** 9 of 10 arms are reached by a behavioural variant; arm 3 is reached by removal only, stated rather than hidden. 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the CORPUS-vs-CLAIM axis turned on a FUNCTION rather than a tool: a helper's JSDoc is a CLAIM about its corpus exactly as a banner is. `gateOf` says "clause" and returns "row tail" — and because the two coincide on short rows, it was right for years and wrong only where the prose got long. ASK WHETHER A HELPER'S NAME AND ITS SLICE AGREE, and when they cannot be made to agree cheaply, REPORT THE GAP RATHER THAN GUESSING A BOUNDARY.** ⓘ A practical mitigation any fire can use today at zero cost: **put the `GATE:` clause LAST in a row**, so the tail and the clause coincide by construction. GATE: none — this row is a completion, cured and guarded in the same fire.
