ame false-signal shape F-1636-4 exists to kill, one level down. The amended clause says **resolve it, never paste it** (iterate `~/.nvm/versions/node/*/bin/codex`, require `--version` ≥ 0.144.1, invoke through `node` because the bash gate refuses a direct binary path — also measured s1640). **GATE: none — this row asks the owner for NOTHING and removes F-1631-3 from the desk.**
- 🟢 **[F-1635-3] ~~BEFORE YOU SPEND A CENT ON F-1631-3, TRY THE FREE REMEDY THE SERVER NAMED~~ → ⛔ **SUPERSEDED s1636 BY F-1636-4 (ABOVE): the wall is LIFTED and no purchase is needed. This row's refutation of the VERSION theory was correct FOR THE RUNNER and is kept for provenance; what it missed is that the PROBE runs a different, genuinely-too-old binary. Read F-1636-4 first.** ⛔ **SELF-REFUTED WITHIN THE SAME FIRE. DO NOT ACT ON THE STRUCK-THROUGH RECOMMENDATION BELOW; IT IS KEPT ONLY BECAUSE THE WAY IT BROKE IS THE FINDING.** ✅ **THE CORRECTED RESULT: `codex --version` IS A MISLEADING INSTRUMENT — IT REPORTS THE npm WRAPPER, NOT THE BINARY THAT EXECUTES, AND THE EXECUTING BINARY WAS NEVER OUT OF DATE.** Measured s1635: `npm ls -g @openai/codex` = **0.133.0** and `codex --version` = `codex-cli 0.133.0`, but **every actual run banner says `OpenAI Codex v0.145.0`** — verified in THREE independent run logs (`20260810-160522` lane-c, `20260810-181709` lane-a, `20260810-183445` lane-b). **0.145.0 is ABOVE the `0.144.1` floor `lane-runner-v3.sh:172` names for knowing 5.6 ids.** 🔑 **DECISIVE: the run that RAISED this wall (`20260810-160522`) was itself executing v0.145.0 and died on *"You've hit your usage limit … try again at Aug 16th, 2026 3:30 AM"* — a QUOTA message from an already-current client.** ➡️ **THEREFORE: the version theory is REFUTED, `npm i -g @openai/codex@latest` would change nothing operationally, and F-1631-3's ORIGINAL quota reading is the correct one. The owner's choice is genuinely just (a) buy credits or (b) wait for 2026-08-16 03:30 — there is no free third door.** ⚠️ **This also retires s1632's own hedge**, which cited the same `codex --version` = 0.133.0 against the 0.144.1 comment and inferred *"the installed CLI could not address the 5.6 ids anyway"*; that inference rests on the same bad instrument and should not be carried forward. 📐 **THE REUSABLE SHAPE — it is F-1632-1's lesson a second time, and I walked into it while writing up F-1632-1's lesson: a probe that shares a defaulted parameter with the subject stops measuring the subject.** There the default was the MODEL; here it is the BINARY — `codex --version` answers about the npm package while `codex exec` runs something else. **Ask the artifact the factory actually produced (the run-log banner), not the tool's self-report.** I caught it only because the SEA-1 dispatch log printed `v0.145.0` two minutes after I had written `0.133.0` onto the owner's desk. **GATE: none owed — this row now ASKS the owner for nothing; it hands F-1631-3 back unchanged.** ⓘ The struck-through original, for provenance: ~~**BEFORE YOU SPEND A CENT ON F-1631-3, TRY THE FREE REMEDY THE SERVER ITSELF NAMED — IT HAS NEVER BEEN ATTEMPTED (measured s1635, ~18:35 local).**~~ I ran the wall file's prescribed second probe, `codex exec -m gpt-5.6-sol "reply exactly: OK"` → status 1, **HTTP 400: *"The 'gpt-5.6-sol' model requires a newer version of Codex. Please upgrade to the latest app or CLI and try again."*** ⚠️ **Read what is NOT in that message: there is no usage-limit language at all.** F-1631-3 was raised on a `You've hit your usage limit … try again at Aug 16th` string and concluded *quota, wait six days*; the direct per-model probe three hours later returns a **VERSION** error naming exactly one remedy. ✅ **MEASURED: `codex --version` = `0.133.0` · `npm view @openai/codex version` = `0.147.0` · `lane-runner-v3.sh:172`'s own comment says *"CLI 0.144.1 knows 5.6 ids"*.** The installed CLI is **below the version the runner itself records as the floor for addressing 5.6 ids**, and 14 minors behind latest. ➡️ **RECOMMENDATION: run `npm i -g @openai/codex@latest` and re-probe, BEFORE buying credits.** It costs nothing, it is reversible (pin back to `0.133.0`), and if it works the *"wait until 2026-08-16"* premise dissolves — waiting would have bought nothing. ⚖️ **HONEST LIMIT, so this is not over-sold: an upgrade may be NECESSARY without being SUFFICIENT.** s1632's probe 3 captured the server's available-models list with **no 5.6 family at all**, which an upgrade will not change if the true cause is an account entitlement. So this is a **cheap experiment to run first, not a diagnosis** — but the experiment has a free downside and a six-day upside. 🚫 **NOT taken by this fire, deliberately:** three lane runs (ap16-1/2/3 on lanes a/c/d) were LIVE at probe time and the runner spawns `codex` per task, so swapping the implementer binary mid-run risks three live runs; it is also an ops change to Robin's machine rather than a repo change, which §7.3 reserves for the owner. **GATE: owner's word (or an attended session with the lanes idle). Recorded in full in `tasks/CODEX-WALL`; the wall itself STAYS and dispatch continues on `gpt-5.5`.**
