ng. The wall file now prescribes `-m` on both models and states which one it is actually about. 📐 **The general shape (`a-probe-that-dies-in-your-stub` class): when a probe and the subject share a defaulted parameter, the probe stops being a measurement of the subject.** The discriminator cost one command. 🚫 **NOT a licence to lower the house default:** `gpt-5.6-sol` remains the owner's ruling (2026-07-10) and F-1631-3 remains OPEN and owner-only — buying credits may still be worth Sol-tier quality before 2026-08-16. What this finding removes is only the *idleness*, not the choice. **GATE: none owed to the owner — the routing header is a documented per-master mechanism, no default was changed and nothing was purchased. Reversible with one word (re-raise the full wall, empty the queue).**
